"""
Convergence Signal & Backtest Engine
-------------------------------------
Cross-sectional equity/crypto scanner that builds a rolling state vector
per symbol (return lags, realized vol, log volume, ATR), then scores each
name on three axes: curvature (eigenvalue decay of the rolling covariance,
i.e. how "compressed" the recent state has been), momentum (projection of
today's state onto the top momentum subspace from an SVD), and anomaly
(robust Mahalanobis distance of today's state from its recent history).
The three are blended into a single "conv" (convergence) score, ranked
cross-sectionally, and used to drive a simple fixed-risk long-only
backtest with ATR-based stops/targets.

Colab usage:
    Paste this whole file into one cell and run. The leading !pip line is
    Colab/IPython syntax, not Python -- running this file with `python
    convergence.py` will fail on it. Delete that line to run outside a
    notebook.

NOTE: Feature windows, score weights, and the long/momentum thresholds
are hand-set, not fitted. Nothing here has been walk-forward validated
or checked for overfitting to the 2023-07 -> present sample. Treat the
backtest metrics as a sanity check on plumbing, not a tested edge.
"""

